#X text 20 220 mlre - live cutting with cir~ (after mlr / mlre for norns);
#X text 20 260 TRACK ROW (left to right);
#X text 20 280 cells 0-15 : click = jump there and play. lit cell = playhead \, f 110;
#X text 20 300 play : start / stop (resumes where it stopped);
#X text 20 320 rec : record the input onto the track (overdub);
#X text 20 340 semi : pitch + speed in semitones -24..24 (12 = 2x faster);
#X text 20 360 rev : play backwards;
#X text 20 380 lo / hi : loop only between these two cells (0-15);
#X text 20 400 len : clip length in seconds (max ~30). load sets it;
#X text 20 420 level : track volume;
#X text 20 440 pre : old audio kept when recording (1 = keep all / 0 = replace) \, f 110;
#X text 20 460 pan : left <-> right;
#X text 20 480 filter : 3 buttons = off / lowpass / highpass;
#X text 20 500 cutoff : filter frequency (26 Hz .. 20 kHz);
#X text 20 520 grp : 1-9 = tracks in the same group stop each other (0 = none) \, f 110;
#X text 20 540 load : open a sound file into the track;
#X text 20 560 clear : erase the tracks audio;
#X text 20 600 PATTERNS (P1-P4) record your cell clicks and loop them;
#X text 20 620 left button steps through: empty -> rec -> play -> stop -> play ... \, f 110;
#X text 20 640 right button: clear. the box shows the state;
#X text 20 680 MIXER;
#X text 20 700 in : level of the inlets into all tracks;
#X text 20 720 out : output volume;
#X text 20 740 dsp : audio on/off;
#X text 20 780 inlets: left + right audio in (mixed to mono);
#X text 20 800 outlets: left + right audio out;
#X text 20 820 all send names are local to this copy (prefixed with its own number) so several copies run side by side \, f 110;
#X obj 20 860 inlet~;
#X obj 100 860 inlet~;
#N canvas 100 100 560 300 engine 0;
#X obj 20 20 inlet~;
#X obj 70 20 inlet~;
#X obj 20 50 +~;
